        "pull_request": {
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/homarr-labs/homarr/pulls/6510",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/homarr-labs/homarr/pull/6510",
          "diff_url": "https://github.com/homarr-labs/homarr/pull/6510.diff",
          "patch_url": "https://github.com/homarr-labs/homarr/pull/6510.patch",
          "merged_at": "2026-08-22T08:53:26Z"
        },
        "body": "## Changes\n\n- Fixes #6082 by averaging Unraid CPU utilization across the logical CPU entries returned by the metrics API, including an empty-list guard.\n- Fixes #6416 by preserving the browser context menu for app and bookmark widgets in view mode while keeping Homarr actions available in edit mode.\n- Fixes #6080 by ignoring scrollbar-sized width oscillations while still recalculating for meaningful width and dynamic-section height changes.\n- Documents the app and bookmark context-menu behavior.\n\n## Scope cleanup\n\nThe OIDC change for #5716 was removed so it can be handled separately with its SSO documentation and review surface.\n\nThe Beszel change for #6024 was removed because it only wrapped authentication JSON, while the report points to a larger collection response. A focused malformed-response check also confirmed the existing integration error decorator already classifies both authentication and collection JSON failures as parse errors; the proposed wrapper downgraded authentication failures to unknown errors.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `pnpm turbo typecheck --filter=@homarr/nextjs --filter=@homarr/integrations --filter=@homarr/docs`\n- Focused `oxfmt` check on changed files\n- Focused `oxlint` on changed TypeScript files\n- Focused malformed Beszel auth and collection response diagnostic",
